  "dependencyFindings": [
    {
      "topic": "audio/winmm",
      "sourceFile": "dlls/winmm/waveform.c",
      "status": "semantic-rebase-required",
      "findings": [
        "Upstream WinMM no longer has WINMM_GetSupportedFormats initialization probes; it advertises legacy PCM masks with a different format-mapping path. Do not import the old lazy probe patch without checking actual format support semantics.",
        "Upstream already uses an InitOnce callback with a different signature and owns the MMDevice enumerator differently.",
        "The old Cider publication lock added by 0008 is absent; 0014 cannot be applied as if that exact old dependency cycle still exists. New callback/worker lock behavior still requires a separate review and runtime evidence."
      ],
      "acceptedAsEquivalent": false,
      "runtimeVerified": false
    },
    {
      "topic": "sync/msync",
      "status": "dependency-audit-only",
      "acceptedAsEquivalent": false,
      "runtimeVerified": false,
      "files": {
        "server/inproc_sync.c": {
          "upstreamSHA256": "0e7173cc883a2ee1d319608c2e1ac8f1a1411398486b7f253974e2fbb55651ac",
          "cxOracleSHA256": "79009f53d087430a5b41efbc9e5b645f5ec55cf1438bebd260a7ed756f14899f"
        },
        "server/object.h": {
          "upstreamSHA256": "62374414bb40ab7a289fbd32ec1feaf44eece37f550f904232087e9f7f4af74c",
          "cxOracleSHA256": "4eeb93c65b13544bde8d4635f0fdd0df71b072be2b990e07394b0547fdc21904"
        },
        "server/protocol.def": {
          "upstreamSHA256": "100fa300a1792da89feb3d62606ffe6223c72ced737ed47cd22a66c8753ca6a0",
          "cxOracleSHA256": "efcfc4fef3a0e2c02ada7eeae79a32cc947b1537d4f218caad220b2a6bac3c2b"
        },
        "dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c": {
          "upstreamSHA256": "882b5023241fcb5204e38a4da0899421370ad718049e5db35662f78cf71068c8",
          "cxOracleSHA256": "4e3345b1f8fdd5ffe33bd2494489058ec9e722b2bb1f987ff5052791200a08a6"
        }
      },
      "findings": [
        "Both bases already use get_sync and the inproc synchronization cache; preserve upstream ownership/access checks rather than introducing parallel per-object hooks.",
        "Upstream server inproc_sync.c uses designated object_ops initializers. Rebase the macOS backend against this layout; do not copy the older positional initializer.",
        "CX transports a shared-memory index in get_inproc_sync_fd replies while upstream only transports an fd. Server protocol, client receive/close paths and generated tables must change together; no literal CX protocol version transplant.",
        "CX msync_wait_objs takes BOOLEAN wait_any; upstream linux_wait_objs takes WAIT_TYPE. Preserve WaitAny/WaitAll/WaitAll-one-object and APC status semantics explicitly.",
        "Highball0005 yield requires the actual msync backend and matching server fallback; the yield-only patch is not an implementation of macOS inproc synchronization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "graphics/d3d9-gl",
      "status": "upstream-primary-behavior-inspected",
      "files": [
        "dlls/wined3d/directx.c",
        "dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c"
      ],
      "findings": [
        "Fixed upstream AUTO selects OpenGL and explicit Vulkan remains explicit.",
        "Unlike the old Highball patch, upstream does not try Vulkan if automatic OpenGL adapter creation fails. This difference has not been changed or accepted as exact fallback equivalence."
      ],
      "runtimeVerified": false
    }
  ],
